    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d133">

                <pb facs="0136" n="124" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg124"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.20/100: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-03-09T14:00:00-04:00">March 9, 1943—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>356. Following received from London: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“1668, March 8, 9 p.m. The Greek ‘army’ in the Middle East has mutinied,
                                Sargent<anchor n="3" xml:id="d133-f1"/> told me this afternoon,
                            following a conversation he had just had with the Prime Minister.
                            Sargent attributed this to ‘Greek politics and Kanellopoulos’<anchor
                                n="4" xml:id="d133-f2"/> recent changes in officer personnel.’ He
                            denied that it was in any sense a revolt against the King and his
                            government. The ‘army’ at present he said consists of two <pb
                                facs="0137" n="125" xml:id="pg125"/> battalions and the third is
                            about to be formed. The Greek Prime Minister has agreed to place the
                            ‘army’ entirely under the jurisdiction and command of General
                                Wilson.”<anchor n="5" xml:id="d133-f3"/>
                        </p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Please report as fully as possible on this subject.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d133-f1" n="3" xml:id="d133-f1-content">
                <p>Sir Orme Garton Sargent, British Deputy Under Secretary of State for Foreign
                    Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d133-f2" n="4" xml:id="d133-f2-content">
                <p>Panayotis Kanellopoulos, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Defense in the
                    Greek Government in Exile.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d133-f3" n="5" xml:id="d133-f3-content">
                <p>Gen. Sir Henry Maitland Wilson, British Commander in Chief, Middle East.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
